WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.216
Last time, we found the right pattern.

2
00:00:03.216 --> 00:00:04.942
Now let's finish the job.

3
00:00:04.942 --> 00:00:09.773
In this lesson, you will learn to complete a COUNTROWS of FILTER measure, label

4
00:00:09.773 --> 00:00:14.260
the result clearly, and check the answer against the data. Let's solve it!

5
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.705
Here is our measure, Bars Category.

6
00:00:18.705 --> 00:00:23.715
COUNTROWS, then FILTER, then the Product table, a comma, and the condition:

7
00:00:23.715 --> 00:00:26.220
Product, Category, equals Bars, in quotes.

8
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.094
Close both brackets and press Enter.

9
00:00:30.094 --> 00:00:32.487
The card shows the answer: eleven.

10
00:00:32.487 --> 00:00:35.280
Eleven products are in the Bars category.

11
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.819
Now a title.

12
00:00:48.819 --> 00:00:54.788
I add a text box above the card, and type: COUNTROWS with Filter. Then a subtitle:

13
00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.280
Number of Bars Category.

14
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.200
Our page now has three groups:

15
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.700
COUNT, DISTINCTCOUNT, and COUNTROWS with FILTER.

16
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.200
Each one answers a different question.

17
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.848
But is eleven correct? Always check.

18
00:01:42.848 --> 00:01:47.860
I open Table view and look at the Product table, with its Category column.

19
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:10.193
Count the Bars in the Category column, or sort the column to group them.

20
00:02:10.193 --> 00:02:11.476
Yes, there are eleven.

21
00:02:11.476 --> 00:02:12.760
Our measure is right!

22
00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.991
Next, I start a new measure for the total cost per box.

23
00:02:59.991 --> 00:03:02.137
Every measure follows the same steps:

24
00:03:02.137 --> 00:03:04.640
write, show, label, and check. Well done!

